name issue_536_loss20_av_sync
describe 20% random loss on a clean 2 Mbps / 50 ms link: video pacer queue grows to seconds and A/V sync drags audio with it
# #536 (Tester): the pacer queue grows to 0.6-2.2 s, video arrives up to 2.4 s late and A/V sync drags audio to
# 0.6-1.1 s mouth-to-ear. Yardstick #792 (#724) ran it on both stacks, 10 seeds: every cell is in the parity band
# (#725), and libwebrtc M157 does the same (mean m2e p95 728 vs ours 613 ms, pacer p95 1529 vs 1117 ms). So these
# lines sit at libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10 (#729); the Tester's stage-2 targets (m2e < 400, video e2e < 1000,
# pacer < 500) are the `stage:later` item #795, not suite lines.
compare_seeds 10
seed 1
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2000kbps delay=50ms loss=20% queue=300ms
# libwebrtc seeds 1-10 (#792): 993 274 1063 792 265 1051 335 137 1473 903 (worst 1473). Ours seed 1: 1042.
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 1474
# libwebrtc: 1.65 1.27 1.59 1.34 1.18 2.06 2.23 1.07 2.29 1.34 (worst 2.29). Ours seed 1: 0.74.
# PR for #894 (the bitrate adjuster runs when the allocation update arrives, as OnBitrateUpdated; on top of #880),
# needs-human: was < 2.3. Ours seed 1: 2.40, past libwebrtc's worst seed (2.29); seeds 1-10 1.81 1.27 1.52 1.20 1.36
# 1.99 1.26 1.32 1.84 1.57 (mean 1.51) on main -> 2.40 1.62 1.55 1.48 1.21 1.83 1.44 1.37 2.12 1.21 (mean 1.62), libwebrtc
# mean 1.60.
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2.45
# libwebrtc: 0 on every seed; longest gap 38-90 ms (worst 90). Ours seed 1: 0, 37.
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.longest_interruption_ms <= 90
# libwebrtc: 2522 910 2519 2441 508 2468 633 442 2744 2570 (worst 2744). Ours seed 1: 2515.
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 2744
# libwebrtc: 1764 670 1581 1751 348 1474 391 318 1603 1828 (worst 1828). Ours seed 1: 1570.
# needs-human (#897, guard rail during a port, program.md 0.2): was < 1829. Send times rounded to the nearest ms
# as the transport's Timestamp::ms() (#897) move ours seed 1 to 1868, past libwebrtc's worst seed; seeds 1-10
# 1868 540 467 324 271 2313 615 285 1671 1801, mean 1015 (was 997; libwebrtc mean 1173).
expect sync.av_offset_p95_ms < 1869
# libwebrtc: freezes 35 24 33 28 17 28 24 27 29 29 (worst 35); total 10016 6909 10278 7519 4593 8464 7549 7690 9193
# 8820 (worst 10278); longest 540 659 634 404 502 747 680 460 795 811 (worst 811). Ours seed 1: 35, 9874, 640.
# Since #873 (no RTT to GoogCC before one is measured, as libwebrtc's aimd_rate_control.cc kDefaultRtt) ours seed 1
# is 11290 and 1178, past libwebrtc's worst seed (10278 / 811); in band on 10 seeds (#873's seed table, parity run
# 41118441708: freeze total 8395 vs libwebrtc 8103, longest 692 vs 623). Window ruling, 2026-10-30, past
# libwebrtc's worst seed (10278 / 811), in band on 10 seeds.
expect video.freeze_count <= 35
expect video.freeze_total_ms <= 11300
expect video.longest_freeze_ms <= 1180
# libwebrtc: 27.13 28.60 27.50 26.67 29.53 27.43 29.00 28.87 26.47 27.23 (worst 26.47). Ours seed 1: 27.3.
# needs-human (#897, guard rail during a port): was > 26.4. Ours seed 1 is now 26.07, past libwebrtc's worst seed;
# seeds 1-10 26.07 28.97 28.27 28.97 29.70 27.07 28.43 29.53 25.90 27.20, mean 28.01 (was 28.27; libwebrtc mean 27.84).
expect video.render_fps > 26.0
# libwebrtc: 211 211 430 969 211 211 452 232 585 211 (worst 969). Ours seed 1: 211.
expect video.time_to_first_frame_ms < 970
# libwebrtc: 0 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 1 0 (worst 4). Ours seed 1: 0.
expect video.keyframe_requests <= 4
# libwebrtc: 11.71 14.07 11.32 10.63 15.57 9.78 17.72 24.63 10.53 13.49 (worst 9.78). Ours seed 1: 11.3.
expect cc.utilization_pct > 9.7
# libwebrtc: 18.82 21.93 19.42 19.88 22.19 18.37 21.07 20.70 20.79 23.05 (worst 23.05). Ours seed 1: 18.5.
expect repair.overhead_pct < 23.1
